  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Stablecoin printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Market Cap near $302.65B (+1.9% 30D) means crypto dollar liquidity did not re-price hard\u2014incremental demand is coming from product and banking-rail headlines rather than a market-cap surge. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/web3/2026-08-26-south-koreas-shinhan-visa-stablecoin-412765\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">South Korea\u2019s Shinhan to use Visa\u2019s stablecoin platform for \u2018future finance\u2019 initiatives</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Stablecoin market structure remains concentration-led:</strong> leadership is still defined by a small set of large issuers/platforms; share shifts matter as much as aggregate market-cap growth. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-08-25-blockchain-association-backs-genius-act-412668\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Blockchain Association backs Treasury\u2019s proposed GENIUS Act rules for stablecoin issuers</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Policy and reserves are resetting issuer priorities:</strong> Issuer and platform share can shift before aggregate market cap does, because policy and reserve quality determine which names institutions will hold. Related: <a href=\"https://news.google.?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hyperliquid Policy Center urges SEC, CFTC to harmonize rules for perpetual contracts</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
